To solve this problem, we can use dynamic programming. The idea is to create a DP table where entry dp[i][j] represents the number of ways to distribute balls from index j to i. We then consider each ball ending at i and keep track of how many ways to distribute balls ending at i-1 to avoid overcounting. We also keep track of the number of 1's and 2's to adjust the skill levels of the dogs during the distribution.

Here's how you can implement it in Python:

